# Adversarial log: www test audit pilot, Phase 3, round 4

Audited head: 74a7213c2. Probe commit: e9ccdac5e.

The F22 loader fix mirrors blog.ts: nothing production-discoverable is
skipped; the loader also sees non-locale directories that production
ignores (ADV-16 note). The F24 hero fix discriminates: a temporary
custom-gradient edit to to-white failed with the named stop. No
tutor-commission K file changed in the phase range.

One real false pass (ADV-15): jsdom pre-resolves var() in computed
background-color from the :root token map and ignores an ancestor's
inline custom property override. A mechanism probe printed the split:
the child's custom property reads #ff0000 while its computed
background-color reads rgb(15, 23, 42). The contrast helper trusts the
pre-resolved value, so the ratio uses the wrong colour. The committed
probe fails its ADV-15 case until Green resolves var() from the element
cascade.

